 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No motif on the prophet of Bani Israel, on fighting, or on the negated wealth (247:21-25). Crown only for the kingship asked for and given (Talut is not a prophet). Title changed from «طلب ملك», which reads as «طلب مَلَك» (asking for an angel) without diacritics. STAGING v4: Their prophet (unnamed in the verse and in both tafsirs) is a blue light drop labelled «نبي» only, no name. The chiefs are an uncountable group in a town (no place is named; town chosen as neutral). No battle: on «تولوا» the chiefs walk away and leave; a few believers (uncountable) remain, sparkle on «قليلا منهم». Talut is a plain faceless man (not a prophet, not the ruler costume: the sources give no detail of his dress), appearing when named; the chiefs point at him in objection; sparkle on «اصطفاه»."
 },
